## Summary
Authored one lesson at `courses/detekcja-obiektow-z-yolo-od-mechaniki-modelu-do-wasnego-detektora-ultralytics-yolo11/lessons/augmentacje-typowe-dla-yolo.json` — validates clean against `LessonSchema`.
**Structure** (m3, 11 min, balanced 0.5 theory/practice ratio → 2 theory beats + 4 widgets):
`theory → dataTable → theory → quiz → code → sandbox`
- **theory** *Po co YOLO syntetyzuje obrazy* — augmentation intuition; mosaic / MixUp / copy-paste, with the MixUp blend formula in KaTeX and the key "boxes travel with pixels" insight. Inline mosaic illustration.
- **dataTable** — cheat-sheet of the three augmentations: what each does, its Ultralytics param + default, when to disable.
- **theory** *close_mosaic i przeliczanie etykiet* — why mosaic/MixUp are switched off in the final epochs, plus the quadrant label-remap formula (KaTeX) that sets up the code task. Inline `close_mosaic` timeline figure.
- **quiz** — targets the "more augmentation is always better / close_mosaic" misconception straight from `research.md`.
- **code** — `place_in_mosaic(box, quadrant)`: pure-numeric, CPU-only YOLO-coordinate exercise (1 visible smoke test + 3 hidden), with full reference solution. Verified the solution passes all four tests.
- **sandbox** — assembles a 2×2 mosaic from four synthetic numpy images and prints the remapped YOLO labels.
**Sources**: 4 entries copied from the `## Augmentacje typowe dla YOLO` block in `sources.md` (Ultralytics aug guide, YOLOv4/mosaic, MixUp, Copy-Paste), with section-level sources on both theory beats.
**Assets**: two illustration PNGs generated locally and cached under `assets/images/` (`mozaika-2x2.png`, `close-mosaic-timeline.png`) — no external image URLs, so the asset gate is satisfied. Prose is in Polish with English technical terms, matching the course convention. No other files touched.
